  "worked_solution": "The minor of ${p}_{32}=3$ (third row, second column) is the determinant of the remaining entries when the column and row containing $3$ are removed: \n\n$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}8 & \u2217 & 4 \\\\ -5 & \u2217 & 6 \\\\ \u2217 & 3 & \u2217\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nSo, the minor of ${p}_{32}=3$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}[\\begin{aligned}8 & 4 \\\\ -5 & 6\\end{aligned}] & =|\\begin{aligned}8 & 4 \\\\ -5 & 6\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =8\\cdot 6-4\\cdot (-5) \\\\  & =48+20 \\\\  & =68.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
